Error / Problem Faced

Potential problems during animation generation include poor source-image cropping, unclear subject information, inconsistent image dimensions, unsuitable driving-video frames, and long processing times for longer videos.

Solution

Kept source images and driving frames at 256 × 256 pixels.
Reviewed relative keypoint displacement and adaptive movement scaling.
Examined the individual processing stages and checked the generated frames and output-video creation process.
Confirmed that the output uses the FPS obtained from the driving video.
